BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Writing\, Editing and Publishing 'The Bloodwood Society'
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T200000
UID:69ce9c85e2a2952aed0c3b27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Everyone has a story to tell\, and there are more ways than
  ever to share your story with the world. But how do you go about collecti
 ng your ideas into a novel? How do you edit it properly so your readers wi
 ll have the best possible experience with it and how do you get your story
  into their hands once your novel is done?\nThis workshop will talk about 
 the creative writing process\, the editing experience\, and the step you'l
 l take to self-publish your first novel. Ainsley Doty shares and talks abo
 ut her creative process and experience writing and self-publishing her fir
 st novel\, The Bloodwood Society.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
