DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T160000
UID:6a135ba1f6bd012f006a0d97@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Capture summer’s beauty forever in this hands-on Flower Pres
 sed Necklace Workshop\, hosted by Gabriela Delworth. Whether you're a jewe
 lry enthusiast or a nature lover\, this session offers a creative space to
  design a wearable piece of art that lasts forever.\nWhat You Will Discove
 r:\nThe Art of Pressing: Learn the essential techniques for preserving blo
 oms\, including the best time of day to harvest and which flower varieties
  hold their color and shape best.\nStorage Secrets: Master the professiona
 l methods for storing pressed flowers to prevent fading and moisture damag
 e.\nJewelry Design: Arrange your choice of delicate petals and greenery in
 to a custom pendant. You will leave with a one-of-a-kind necklace that res
 pects your personal style.\nWorkshop Details:\nAll inclusive: Your free re
 gistration covers all materials\; all participants receive a curated kit b
 y the instructor. Tools are provided by the instructor and returned at the
  end of the workshop.\nSkill Level: Perfect for beginners\; no prior exper
 ience in jewelry making or gardening is required.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a135ba1f6bd012f006a0d97
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
