BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Armchair Travel: African Safari
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T150000
UID:6a511220aa34e23600ee2ea3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Pilot\, adventurer and photographer\, Lola Reid Allin\, tr
 ansports audiences to exotic destinations around the world from the comfor
 t of their chairs.\nFeel Africa seep into your soul as Lola’s photograph
 y captures the hunters’ “Big Five”— lions\, leopards\, elephants\
 , Cape buffalo\, & rhinos — as your safari vehicle bumps across the Se
 rengeti and the Masai Mara. Hang out with a baboon troop in the shadow of
  Mount Kenya. Sleep over with the Masai in a\nmanyatta. Step into history 
 at Karen Blixen’s house\, immortalized in her 1937 memoir\, Out of Afri
 ca. Follow legendary Dian Fossey’s footsteps to observe endangered Mou
 ntain Gorillas\, in Rwanda’s mist-shrouded Virunga Mountains. Travel by
  camel over Tanzania's barren northlands and Morocco's sumptuous\nSahara. 
 Float over the wild savanna in a hot air balloon and paddle a dugout in Bo
 tswana's Okavango Delta.\nRegistration is encouraged\, and we welcome dro
 p in customers until capacity is reached.\nPlease feel free to check out\,
  Lola's book\,\nHighway to the Sky\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a511220aa34e23600ee2ea3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
