BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lead Where You Are: Leadership Skills for Young Professionals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T130000
UID:6a4d7377f1927c2900f740e1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Leadership does not start when you become a manager or directo
 r. It starts with how you show up at work every day. In this workshop\, pa
 rticipants will explore what it means to act like a leader early in their 
 career through confidence\, professionalism\, communication\, and accounta
 bility. We will discuss the key attitudes and habits that help young profe
 ssionals stand out\, build trust\, and make a positive impact in the workp
 lace. Participants will also learn practical ways to navigate everyday wor
 kplace challenges with maturity and confidence. Whether you are starting y
 our career or looking to grow professionally\, this session will help you 
 build the mindset and skills to lead where you are.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d7377f1927c2900f740e1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
