BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grant Writing and Proposal Basics: Arts Mentor in Residence Series
  with Elaine Chan-Dow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T173000
UID:6a3d61f5ed35742f00fe4063@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Writing a strong grant or proposal requires clarity\, organiza
 tion and an understanding of what reviewers are looking for. In this works
 hop on grant writing and proposal basics\, learn how to structure applicat
 ions\, communicate project ideas effectively and strengthen supporting mat
 erials. Peter Kingstone of Toronto Arts Council\, Chelsea Virginia of Eas
 t End Arts and Beth Helmers from Scarborough Arts will join the Q&A to s
 hare grant application tips\, common mistakes and insights to help partici
 pants strengthen their submissions.\nThis program will be followed by a 
 Q&A.\nThis workshop is presented by transdisciplinary artist\, educator an
 d researcher Elaine Chan-Dow\, whose art and research practice explores cu
 lture\, environmental sustainability and contemporary creative practice.
 \nLearn more about the\nArts Mentor in Residence\nprogram\, including work
 shops and one-on-one consultations.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
 y under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The
  information will only be used for event and program registration\, delive
 ry and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informatio
 n can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-59
 81\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d61f5ed35742f00fe4063
