BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Step In\, Stand Out: Navigating Your First 90 Days at Work
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T130000
UID:6a4d6dd051c8395f00feb352@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The first 90 days in a new job set the tone for your long-term
  success and this workshop will equip you to step in with clarity and stan
 d out with confidence. Together\, we will walk through a structured roadma
 p built around five key phases: learning and observation\, relationship-bu
 ilding\, performance and communication excellence\, personal brand and vis
 ibility\, and finally\, a powerful bonus 10-day introspection period to he
 lp you evaluate alignment and ensure the role truly fits you. You will lea
 rn how to adapt to workplace culture\, build authentic relationships\, ask
  smart questions\, and demonstrate value early. By the end\, you will leav
 e with a practical 100-day success plan designed to help you build the nex
 t steps of your career with intention.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d6dd051c8395f00feb352
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
