SUMMARY:Writing Hard Truths: Ethical Issues & Craft Considerations
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T153000
UID:6a2850561e67cd9cb338adb9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How do we tell powerful stories that matter? Stories that expl
 ore family secrets\, confront historical injustices or give voice to margi
 nalized experiences while upholding ethical responsibilities and honoring 
 the complexities of truth?\nAuthor Caroline Topperman\n(Your Roots Cast a 
 Shadow)\nlead this writers' workshop that delves into the intricate proces
 s of writing creative nonfiction that tackles challenging subjects\, parti
 cularly those related to family\, displacement\, estrangement\, and immigr
 ation.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this f
 orm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries 
 Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be use
