SUMMARY:Business Inc. Virtual Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260807T130000
UID:6a5a84e79943bdf31e9fac9d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Fall 2026 Business Inc. Virtual Info Session to learn
  about this 8-week program supporting Toronto entrepreneurs to launch and 
 grow.\nDo you have a small business or idea and want tailored feedback and
  support to take it to the next level? Join the Business Inc. Program to c
 onnect with experienced mentors and other entrepreneurs that will help you
  grow.\nDuring eight weekly sessions\, entrepreneurs will learn business f
 undamentals\, get clarity on the viability of their business ideas\, get f
 eedback and reviews from professional business advisors\, discuss with and
  learn from their peers\, and build a foundation for success.\nA general s
 tream will run weekly at Deer Park branch on Thursday evenings from Octo
 ber 22 – December 10\, from 6 - 9pm.\nA general stream will run weekly a
 t North York Central Library on Tuesday evenings from October 20 – Dec
 ember 8\, from 6 - 9pm.\nThe Newcomer Entrepreneur stream will run weekly
  at Runnymede branch on Wednesday evenings from October 7 – November 25\
 , from 6 - 9pm.\nThe Women Entrepreneur stream will run weekly at S. Walt
 er Stewart branch on Saturdays\, November 14 – December 5\, from 10am -
  4pm.\nJoin us at our Virtual Information Session to learn more about this
  program\, meet the instructor\, and ask any questions you may have about 
 your application.\nLearn about\nBusiness Inc.\n\, an eight-week business p
 rogram offered in partnership with the Toronto Business Development Centre
 .\nRegistration:\nThis virtual Zoom event is free to join. Once registered
 \, you’ll receive an email with the Zoom link.\nNeed help with Zoom?\n-\
 nJoining and participating in a Zoom webinar\n-\nZoom Privacy Statement\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
