BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Turning Red Flags into Strengths: How to Answer Tough Interview Qu
 estions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260806T130000
UID:6a4d6ea383a07530004ae3f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Career gaps\, job changes\, lack of experience\, layoffs\, or 
 difficult transitions do not have to define your story. In this practical 
 and confidence-building workshop\, participants will learn how to answer c
 hallenging resume and interview questions with clarity\, confidence\, and 
 professionalism. We will cover common “red flag” questions and provide
  strategies to reframe challenges into strengths while staying authentic. 
 Through real examples and practical scripts\, participants will gain tools
  to communicate their experiences in a way that builds trust and credibili
 ty. By the end of the session\, attendees will feel more prepared to navig
 ate tough questions and tell their career story with confidence.\nThis pro
 gram is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously suppor
 ted by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fide
 lity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nWilli
 am and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.
 ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d6ea383a07530004ae3f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
