BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Access To Housing: Information Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T160000
UID:69c58e38deee9abd8ee5f145@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you need information about applying for Rent-Geared-to-Inco
 me Housing or assistance with your application? Join Margaret's Housing an
 d Community Support Services staff for drop-in sessions on the 3rd Tuesday
  of each month\, from 2-4pm.\nThis session has been rescheduled from Tuesd
 ay\, August 18 to Tuesday\, September 1.\nThis session will cover:\nAn ove
 rview of the RGI application process\nEligibility requirements\nSteps for 
 submitting and updating applications\nInformation on priority access\nThe 
 choice-based cycle housing offer process and the Single Offer Rule\nFinanc
 ial assistance programs to help the tenants/home owners\nWhether you are a
  first-time applicant or seeking assistance with an existing application\,
  this session will empower you with the knowledge needed to navigate the R
 ent Geared to Income housing system.\nPresented by Margaret's Housing and 
 Community Support Services\, a multi-service agency that provides housing 
 options to women living with mental illness and substance abuse\, and comm
 unity-based support services for individuals experiencing intersectional i
 ssues tied to mental health challenges and homelessness.\nPlease arrive a 
 few minutes early.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 1 (1st floor)
