DESCRIPTION:Enjoy some light refreshments\, and informal discussion about 
 services in the neighbourhood. Get to know your local library staff and le
 t us know what information and resources you would like to access at the l
 ibrary and in the community.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all
  participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nNo Regi
 stration Required.  All are welcome!\nJessie's Centre\nCome meet staff fr
 om Jessie's Centre\, a multi-service drop-in centre that supports young pr
 egnant and parenting women who are 22 and under. Learn about the variety o
 f services Jessie’s Centre provides\, including counselling\, housing\, 
 health\, education\, parenting and personal development groups\, and so mu
 ch more! If you are—or someone you know is—pregnant\, may be pregnant\
 , or parenting\, you can visit the Jessie’s Centre at 205 Parliament Str
 eet or call 416-365-1888 for more information.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First Floor Program Room (CPR)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69f637fa66c3387a9d08a52d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
