BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What's the Worst That Can Happen?: Writing Dystopian Fiction With 
 Rachel A. Rosen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T160000
UID:6a42acb048c98c3600a32cd5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From classics like Margaret Atwood’s\nHandmaid’s Tale\nto 
 modern takes such as Cherie Dimaline’s\nThe Marrow Thieves\nor Catherine
  Hernandez’s\nCrosshairs\n\,       dystopian fiction is a mainstay of Ca
 nadian sci-fi and fantasy. Why do we seek out cautionary tales when the re
 al world is already so bleak? And how can      prospective writers of dyst
 opian speculative fiction write believable\, immersive worlds? Join us for
  a creative writing workshop hosted by Aurora Award nominee and author\, R
 achel A. Rosen! Through a series of activities and guided exercises\, part
 icipants will develop a literary toolbox to deepen their world-building an
 d generate ideas for their own writing. Hosted by the Merril Collection o
 f Science Fiction\, Speculation & Fantasy\nThis event is intended for audi
 ences age 18 and up. Please register for this event on our website as spac
 e is limited.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on
  this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Lib
 raries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only
  be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Que
 stions about how the library handles your information can be directed to A
 nswerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\
 , Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Reading Room\, 3rd floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a42acb048c98c3600a32cd5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Teach Your Kids About Money
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T120000
UID:6a144cb0caf93436005e2f8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From the early years of learning how to count change to budget
 ing in the high school years\, Teri Courchene will share ideas and strateg
 ies for teaching your children the value of money.\nTeri will cover topics
  including how playing board and card games helps children with math\, str
 ategies for giving children allowances\, and giving children more responsi
 bility with money as they get older. She will also cover how to get teenag
 ers started with investing once they turn 18.\nPresented by Teri Courchene
 \, an economist\, math tutor and former investing instructor at the Univer
 sity of Toronto School for Continuing Studies.\nThis program is for adults
  but Teri invites children to attend with their parents.\nRegistration Req
 uired. Spots are limited.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal in
 formation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under th
 e Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informati
 on will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eva
 luation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be d
 irected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Y
 onge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 301
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a144cb0caf93436005e2f8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
