BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Edible History of Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T190000
UID:6a6a0393e9de6536001f01f6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto is a global culinary capital\, home to iconic food bra
 nds and restaurants\, from Café Diplomatico to Mr. Christie's Cookies. Bu
 t how did Toronto earn its reputation as a foodie haven? Join culinary his
 torian Dr. Laura Carlson on a mouth-watering journey through Toronto’s f
 ood history. Bring your appetite and stretchy pants for a virtual taste of
  Toronto's past and present.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welcomed 
 until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall - Located on the 1st Floo
 r
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a0393e9de6536001f01f6
